# INNER-TYPE-AXIS coverage — a USER STRUCT with a droppable field as the
# guarded payload (`Guard[Payload]`, `Payload` carrying a `String`).
#
# The existing guard-get net samples only RUNTIME inner types -- String,
# Vector[int], Vector[String], Dict -- all of which reach a `gorget_*_free`
# through `resource_meta_for`. A user struct is a DIFFERENT droppability
# channel: it becomes droppable by the `gmod.resource_types` transitive-field
# fixpoint, which synthesises a `Payload__drop`. `is_droppable_type`
# (self_host_lowerer/lower_drops.gg:222) has a separate arm for each, so a fix
# that only covered the runtime-resource arm would leave this cell broken --
# which is precisely why sampling one value of the inner-type axis is an
# anecdote and not a net (Core #12).
#
# `g.get()` yields a view INTO the mutex-owned Payload; minting it owned and
# registering it for drop runs `Payload__drop` on the alias, freeing the
# `String` the mutex still owns.
#
# SCOPE — exactly one cell of each axis:
#   inner type   = USER STRUCT with a droppable field (siblings: String /
#                  Vector / Dict runtime resources; Box-shaped pointer inners)
#   destination  = method-receiver / field-read (non-consuming)
#   root shape   = LOCAL mutex (the `&`-param root is a separate filed defect,
#                  known_gaps/mutex_amp_param_lost_writes_and_segv.gg)
#   guard family = Guard (siblings: ReadGuard / WriteGuard)
#
# RED-VERIFIED on the SELF-HOST lane with the pre-fix self-host compiler
# (`GG_IMPL=selfhost scripts/gg_impl.sh`) -- see the commit for the observed
# failure. The Rust lane was already fixed by Track J, so a `cargo test`
# RED-verify would be green before AND after (Core #12's anti-pattern).
#
# HEAP-FORCED VALUE (never a literal -- a rodata String has cap=0, so
# `gorget_string_free` short-circuits and the bug reads as absent).

struct Payload:
    String name

String heaped():
    return "hello " + "world" + "-forced"

void main():
    Mutex[Payload] m = Mutex[Payload](Payload(heaped()))
    Guard[Payload] g = m.lock()
    print(g.get().name)
